Tier 6 -- pseudo-cluster staged integration, shape A (reaper guest).

Three vnet jails as nodes on an internal bridge, real ZFS lineage, real ssh,
real CARP, and a fence driver whose "power off" stops the target jail. Named
stages, individually runnable: substrate, repl, interrupt, promote, carp,
quorum, concurrency, flap, failback, resurrection, hostile (and the M1 loop's
replfail, replconc, replevidence, report, retention, hostileenv). See
TESTING.md §7.

The M3 stages, and what each is for:

    carp         the advskews ARE the succession map. Each node MASTER for its
                 own identity and BACKUP for the ones it may inherit, applied
                 from what `seance verify --render carp` printed and read back
                 by `verify`.
    quorum       an isolated node is not a dead node. It freezes at rung 2 and
                 fences nobody, while the connected heir succeeds it.
    concurrency  two heirs told about one death at the same instant; exactly
                 one acts, and the loser is stopped by CARP first and by the
                 claim check afterwards.
    flap         a link that comes back inside the debounce window. Rung 1
                 re-reads CARP, finds the transition gone, and nothing changes.

WHAT SHAPE A CANNOT PROVE ABOUT M3, stated so nobody looks for it here: devd(8)
is KEYWORD: nojail and does not run in a vnet jail, so the rules are rendered,
installed and recognised by `verify` but never FIRE. Every CARP stage therefore
invokes `seance promote-event <vhid>@<if>` itself -- the same command the rule's
action names -- and the firing is tier 8's, measured by docs/DRILLS.md
drill-node as T1 to T2.

The substrate itself lives in tests/cluster/lib/cluster.subr and is asserted
by t_substrate.sh (stage 'substrate'): jails up, ssh mesh, delegated ZFS,
send/recv between jails, isolation, stop/start, teardown cleanliness,
up-down-up idempotence. Every later stage is entitled to assume all of that
and asserts none of it again.

Stage selection:

    SEANCE_STAGES=substrate,repl sh tests/run.sh   # a subset
    sh tests/run.sh                                # every stage

An unset or empty SEANCE_STAGES means all stages. A name that is not a known
stage is a contract error (exit 2), not a silent skip -- see
tests/cluster/lib/stage.subr, which each t_*.sh sources and calls
stage_begin <name> from before doing anything expensive.

These tests need root, ZFS, vnet jails and the reaper guest's own userland;
they do not run on the workstation.

Files named t_*.sh are tests; anything else here is ignored.
